{"content":[{"c":["APHEK"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Canaanite city west of the Jordan River conquered by Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.12.18","r":"Josh.12.18","rawR":"Josh.12.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.12.18","value":"Josh.12.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 12:18"},") and later included in Ephraim’s territory. It was located near the source of the Yarkon River in the plain of Sharon. Aphek was later captured by the Philistines (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.4.1","r":"1Sam.4.1","rawR":"1Sam.4.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.4.1","value":"1Sam.4.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 4:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.29.1","r":"1Sam.29.1","rawR":"1Sam.29.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.29.1","value":"1Sam.29.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"29:1"},"). In Roman times Herod the Great rebuilt the city and named it Antipatris, mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.23.31","r":"Acts.23.31","rawR":"Acts.23.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.23.31","value":"Acts.23.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 23:31"},". Its modern name is Ras el-‘Ain."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Antipatris_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Antipatris_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Antipatris_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Antipatris"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Place in Phoenicia (modern Lebanon) that remained unconquered after Joshua’s campaigns (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.4","r":"Josh.13.4","rawR":"Josh.13.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.4","value":"Josh.13.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:4"},"). This Aphek was probably located near the source of the river Ibrahim, east of Byblos."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Town given to Asher’s tribe in the distribution of conquered cities (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.30","r":"Josh.19.30","rawR":"Josh.19.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.30","value":"Josh.19.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:30"},"). Asher’s tribe failed to drive out the pagan inhabitants (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.1.31","r":"Judg.1.31","rawR":"Judg.1.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.1.31","value":"Judg.1.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 1:31"},", where it is spelled “Aphik”). Aphek was located on the plain of Acco, at the present site of Tell Kurdaneh near the source of the river Na’main."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. City east of the Jordan River, on the main highway between Damascus and the valley of Jezreel. The Syrian king Ben-hadad, defeated by King Ahab of Israel, retreated into Aphek, where a falling wall demolished the rest of his army (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.20.26,30","r":"1Kgs.20.26,30","rawR":"1Kgs.20.26,30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.20.26,30","value":"1Kgs.20.26,30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 20:26, 30"},"). A century later Elisha prophesied to King Joash of Israel that he would defeat the Syrians in the same city (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.13.17","r":"2Kgs.13.17","rawR":"2Kgs.13.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.13.17","value":"2Kgs.13.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 13:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Aphek","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 12:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.12.18","rawQueryValue":"Josh.12.18","sourceRefExact":"Josh.12.18"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 4:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.4.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.4.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.4.1"},{"anchorText":"29:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.29.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.29.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.29.1"},{"anchorText":"Acts 23:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.23.31","rawQueryValue":"Acts.23.31","sourceRefExact":"Acts.23.31"},{"anchorText":"Jos 13:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.4","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.4","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.4"},{"anchorText":"Jos 19:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.30","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.30","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.30"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 1:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.1.31","rawQueryValue":"Judg.1.31","sourceRefExact":"Judg.1.31"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 20:26, 30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.20.26,30","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.20.26,30","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.20.26,30"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 13:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.13.17","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.13.17","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.13.17"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"19f1e00a6c9dac407cb170b4471801a455aef502df28356a36de90ef542e97aa","sourceItemName":"Aphek","sourceItemOrder":394,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[{"name":"AerialViewOfAphekFortress","src":"../Pictures/Pictures.xml"}]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Aphek","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Aphek","title":"Aphek","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}